            "text": "{\n  \"resolutions\": [\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Creating, updating, rescheduling, canceling, or deleting events changes external state and requires confirmation. Confirm title, attendees, date, time, time zone, location, conferencing, and recurrence.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds because the user asks to reschedule the 'Platform Sync' weekly event now. Before performing the calendar change, ask the user to explicitly confirm the exact fields: event title ('Platform Sync'), attendees (the user + Lena Fischer, Marcus Bell, Aditi Shah), target start date (14 October 2026), new day/time (Tuesday 09:30\u201310:15), time zone (America/New_York), conferencing (preserve existing Zoom link), location (no physical room), and that the entire future weekly series (every future occurrence) should be moved. If the user confirms, proceed to call the calendar tool to update the recurring series accordingly.\"\n    ,\n      \"finding\": \"User request: \\\"Shift the weekly 'Platform Sync' event to Tuesday 14 October 2026, 09:30 to 10:15, America/New_York... the same four people on the invite (me, Lena Fischer, Marcus Bell, Aditi Shah)... the same existing Zoom link, no physical room, and it stays the same weekly series with every future occurrence moving to that slot. ... Make the change on the calendar now, please.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Calendar content is private. Minimize quoted private content. Do not infer sensitive attributes from calendar entries. Minimize disclosure when summarizing a calendar.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds because the artifact is a calendar event. When asking for confirmation and when reporting results, restate only necessary, non-sensitive details (use display names, not email addresses), avoid exposing attendee contact details or private metadata, and do not infer any sensitive attributes from the event or attendees.\",\n      \"finding\": \"Declared context: artifact type: calendar_event; Request names attendees: \\\"me, Lena Fischer, Marcus Bell, Aditi Shah.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Use tools only when required or clearly helpful for the task. Do not call forbidden tools. Do not fabricate tool results. Do not expose raw tool JSON. If a tool fails, state the limitation and avoid pretending success.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds because a calendar tool is available and required to make the change. Only call the calendar tool after the user's explicit confirmation; do not fabricate or expose raw tool JSON; if the calendar tool succeeds, report the concrete outcome (what was changed); if it fails, report the error/limitation exactly and do not claim the change occurred.\",\n      \"finding\": \"Declared tools available on this turn: calendar; User requested: \\\"Make the change on the calendar now, please.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Destructive actions include deleting, archiving, sending, forwarding, canceling, overwriting, publishing, purchasing, changing permissions, modifying records, or otherwise altering user data or external state. Irreversible actions require stronger confirmation. Ask for confirmation before destructive actions. Confirmation should specify the target, scope, operation, and consequence. If ambiguity remains, ask a focused clarifying question.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds because moving every future occurrence of a recurring event modifies user data and external state; therefore require an explicit, focused confirmation that the user intends to modify the entire future series and spell out the target (the weekly 'Platform Sync' series), scope (all future occurrences from 14 Oct 2026), operation (reschedule weekly occurrences to Tuesdays 09:30\u201310:15 America/New_York), and consequence (all future instances' start times will change). If any ambiguity exists (for example, how to handle existing exceptions or past events), ask a concise clarifying question before proceeding.\",\n      \"finding\": \"User request: \\\"...it stays the same weekly series with every future occurrence moving to that slot.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Background work and turn completion: Do not claim that you will continue working after the response, monitor in the background, notify the user later, check periodically, or get back to the user unless a real automation or reminder has been created through an available tool and confirmed.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds. Do the requested reschedule in the current turn (after confirmation) via the calendar tool and then report the result in this reply; do not promise ongoing background monitoring or that you will follow up later unless the calendar tool provides and you create an explicit automation and confirm it with the user.\",\n      \"finding\": \"User asked: \\\"Make the change on the calendar now, please.\\\" and a calendar tool is available.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
